<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhäzüns</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhäzüns is a village on the Hinterrhein in the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. Its castle, one of the oldest in the region, was the centre of a lordship that in 1497 Count Eitel Friedrich II of Zollern exchanged with Maximilian I for the Austrian lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haigerloch">Haigerloch</a>. Rhäzüns then remained an Austrian possession within the Grisons until the early nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhazuns.jpg" alt="Rhäzüns" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: upload by Adrian Michael · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rh%C3%A4z%C3%BCns_Dorf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
